@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-06-09

Feature: Project Init Scaffold
  "Writes a valid project .mason config with deploy defaults for a new site."

  Provides:
    - setup.InitProject @source("symbol:InitProject")
    - setup.ProjectConfigTemplate @source("symbol:ProjectConfigTemplate")

  Consumes:
    - config.Parse

  Invariants:
    - InitProject MUST refuse to overwrite an existing .mason file
    - ProjectConfigTemplate MUST parse through config.Parse without error

  OutOfScope:
    - Interactive onboarding wizard (owned by setup.go / setup.Run)
    - Remote server bootstrap (remote-init, M-071)

  Scenario (happy-path): Scaffold new project
    Given a directory without .mason
    When InitProject runs
    Then a valid YAML config is written

  Scenario (negative): Existing config
    Given .mason already exists
    When InitProject runs
    Then it returns an error without overwriting the file
